  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A stoppered clay vial of bitter green cordial, found among the web-wrapped effects of a traveller who never left the temple. The label, in a tidy, careful hand, reads only: <em>“One swallow, seventh-day, as ever. — Selma.”</em></p><p>Whoever drinks a swallow sleeps utterly without dreams for the next seven nights. No apothecary could name any other virtue in it — nor say why anyone would brew such a thing, or take it <em>as ever</em>.</p>",
